media: sun50i-h713-hdmirx: switch the capture back on instead of switching the source

Two things were wrong in the re-arm that 0119 left behind.

The wait used h713_hdmirx_signal_present(), which watches the AFBD flip
pointers. Those move from the plane side too, so the driver reported "the
firmware released it" 12 ms after a republication while the capture enable was
still clear and the wall stayed black. Watch the enable itself.

And waiting is not enough: measured over 30 s after a republication, bit 31 of
0x06940928 never comes back on its own. So set it -- both enables, luma and
chroma, which is exactly what the firmware's memory_agent_onoff does for its
mask 0x008. Doing that from the ARM was measured on 2026-09-07: the bits stay
set, the flip pointers move, the picture comes up, and the window chain keeps
the geometry the first rebuild computed.

That is the whole point. The source switch also brings the capture back, and it
is still there as the fallback, but it makes the firmware rebuild its window
chain a second time and that pass shrinks the capture by two thirds
(doku/nachtlog/S7). Writing two bits does not.

The block stays read-only otherwise. These two enables are named and commented
as the exception, with the measurement that justifies it.

diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c	2026-09-07 22:54:21.503730618 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c	2026-09-07 22:54:21.511438316 +0200
@@ -179,6 +179,22 @@
 #define H713_INCAP_TOTAL	0x548
 
 /*
+ * The capture output enables, one for luma and one for chroma. Bit 31 of each
+ * is what the firmware's memory_agent_onoff clears for its mask 0x008
+ * (re/notes/color-csc-blocker.md), and clearing it is how a descriptor
+ * publication stops the capture: the frame counter at +0x104 keeps running and
+ * nothing is written, so the wall holds its last picture.
+ *
+ * These two are the exception to the read-only rule above, and it is measured,
+ * not assumed: setting bit 31 from the ARM on 07.09.2026 brought the capture
+ * back, the bits stayed set, the flip pointers moved and the picture came up.
+ * Nothing else in the block is written.
+ */
+#define H713_INCAP_ENABLE_Y	0x928
+#define H713_INCAP_ENABLE_C	0x968
+#define H713_INCAP_ENABLE_BIT	BIT(31)
+
+/*
  * The capture ring. Three Y slots and three C slots, fixed by the firmware;
  * the slot pitch is 0x1ff000 and C slot i is Y slot i plus 0x5fd000. Y and C
  * always name the same index in every dump taken so far. Measured on the
@@ -1528,15 +1544,21 @@
 /*
  * Wait for the firmware to hand the capture back by itself.
  * Returns true if it did.
+ *
+ * The criterion is the capture enable, not the flip pointers: those move from
+ * the plane side as well and say nothing about whether the capture is writing.
+ * Using them here cost a debugging round -- the driver reported success while
+ * the picture stayed black.
  */
 static bool h713_hdmirx_wait_enable(struct h713_hdmirx *rx, const char *why)
 {
 	ktime_t start = ktime_get();
+	unsigned int val;
 
 	do {
-		if (h713_hdmirx_signal_present(rx)) {
-			dev_info(rx->dev,
-				 "Freigabe: %s, nach %lld ms\n",
+		if (!regmap_read(rx->incap, H713_INCAP_ENABLE_Y, &val) &&
+		    (val & H713_INCAP_ENABLE_BIT)) {
+			dev_info(rx->dev, "Freigabe: %s, nach %lld ms\n",
 				 why, ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get(), start));
 			return true;
 		}
@@ -1545,6 +1567,28 @@
 	return false;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Switch the capture output back on, the way the firmware's own memory_agent
+ * does it: bit 31 in both enables. Measured to work from the ARM and to stick.
+ *
+ * This is what a republished descriptor needs instead of a source switch. The
+ * switch also brings the capture back, but it makes the firmware run its whole
+ * window rebuild a second time, and that pass loses the geometry -- the capture
+ * ends up 2/3 short and the picture is a smeared band (doku/nachtlog/S7).
+ */
+static int h713_hdmirx_capture_enable(struct h713_hdmirx *rx)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(rx->incap, H713_INCAP_ENABLE_Y,
+				 H713_INCAP_ENABLE_BIT, H713_INCAP_ENABLE_BIT);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = regmap_update_bits(rx->incap, H713_INCAP_ENABLE_C,
+					 H713_INCAP_ENABLE_BIT,
+					 H713_INCAP_ENABLE_BIT);
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static void h713_hdmirx_rearm(struct h713_hdmirx *rx)
 {
 	bool erste = !rx->desc_seen;
@@ -1578,11 +1622,17 @@
 	 * is wrong -- and the log says which of the two happened.
 	 */
 	if (!erste) {
-		if (h713_hdmirx_wait_enable(rx, "Firmware hat selbst freigegeben, kein Quellenwechsel noetig"))
+		int ret = h713_hdmirx_capture_enable(rx);
+
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(rx->dev,
+				 "Freigabe: Capture-Freigabe nicht schreibbar: %d\n",
+				 ret);
+		else if (h713_hdmirx_wait_enable(rx, "Capture direkt freigegeben, kein Quellenwechsel"))
 			return;
 
 		dev_warn(rx->dev,
-			 "Freigabe: Firmware hat nach %u ms nicht selbst freigegeben; Quellenwechsel als Rueckfall -- der baut die Fensterkette neu und verliert dabei die Geometrie (doku/nachtlog/S7)\n",
+			 "Freigabe: direkte Freigabe hat nach %u ms nicht gegriffen; Quellenwechsel als Rueckfall -- der baut die Fensterkette neu und verliert dabei die Geometrie (doku/nachtlog/S7)\n",
 			 H713_REARM_TIMEOUT_MS);
 	}
 
